    "relation": "discusses",
    "tranche": "T6",
    "tranche_reason": "The study trains SAEs at different dictionary widths, but does not match features across widths or measure whether larger-dictionary features split, partition inputs, or form nearby directions. Its results do not test the stated claim versions.",
    "gate_note": "The width ablation reports reconstruction error, dictionary utilization, coherence and label entropy, but none measures feature splitting or cross-dictionary correspondence. The raw-dimension, PCA and random-direction comparisons address retrieval coherence, not the claim versions, so they are not included as rows.",
    "test_reason": "The study trains BatchTopK and vanilla SAEs on CONCH and UNI2-h pathology embeddings at widths 1024–4096, but reports only aggregate reconstruction, alive fraction, coherence and entropy per width. It never matches features across widths, measures splitting, partitioning, absorption, hierarchy or decomposition. So it does not test any version. It is not T4 either, since it does not rely on splitting as a tool.",
    "authors_conclusion": "Correct. The authors conclude SAEs yield coherent, label-enriched latents for histopathology embeddings that should be treated as candidate concepts for expert assessment. They draw no conclusions about feature splitting.",
    "recipe": "close",
    "recipe_differences": "The study trains SAEs at multiple widths on the same histopathology embedding dataset, but compares aggregate reconstruction and feature statistics rather than aligning features or measuring splits. It uses BatchTopK and vanilla L1 variants.",
    "method_sensitivity": "",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "At target L0=64, raising CONCH SAE width from 1024 to 4096 lowered NMSE 0.0141→0.0115, cut alive fraction 32.1%→16.7%, and left top-32 coherence ~0.83 and entropy 0.101→0.090 (Table 5).",
        "proposed_claim": "In pathology-embedding SAEs, wider dictionaries improve reconstruction but leave most added latents dead, with per-feature coherence roughly unchanged; cross-width feature relations are not measured.",
        "row_ids": [
          "r1",
